cation can also  be used for conjugate  primarily looking at conjugate width  position and even concentration  besides dispensing vision qc  is also important during lamination  primarily  for  position and overlap  because  if the overlap is too great for example  in building up a lateral flow device  a test line can be lost or a control  line can be lost  and when considering reagent deposition  and vision  and quality control  it's important to put them in context  of batch production and inline  production  for batch production  materials are typically pre-cut to  length  membrane can be pre-laminated prior to  reagent deposition or the individual  layers  can be processed before lamination  batch production usually is in the  context of r d  to low level production typically less  than one million tests per year  developed  quality control  while sometimes automated is usually  manual  this is a picture of a batch level  system  for reagent deposition  capable of depositing antibodies on  nitrocellulose and spraying gold  conjugate through an air jet  any sample pad pre-treatment or blocking  and sometimes even conjugate  impregnation is accomplished using some  type of tray for dipping  and all materials are dried in an oven  drying is typically the rate limiting  stop  a small laminator is used to assemble  the test  to make layers as shown to the left  and a guillotine cutter is used to cut  strips to the desired length  often the goal is to start in batch  level manufacturing and once a process  is set to move to larger scale  production  however there are many things to  consider  in this transition  first of all material selection  oftentimes and this is true in cobit 19  testing  certain materials are chosen for  higher sensitivity results  however these materials are often  brittle thin and sometimes have  poor tensile strength  when considering inline manufacturing  sometimes hundred meter rolls of  materials need to be tracked  so tensile strength is 